148","actor_text":"President, by Ex. Ord. No. 14148","date_basis":"printed_next_to_acting_instrument","from":"current-law@jobs/current-law/output","from_job":"current-law","ids":["usc:ev:ed26dd442844"],"mechanism_text":"revocation (as stated in an OLRC note at 23 U.S.C. 101 note)","quote":"Ex. Ord. No. 14052, Nov. 15, 2021, 86 F.R. 64335, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 14082, § 4(c), Sept. 12, 2022, 87 F.R. 56863, which related to implementation of the Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act (Pub. L. 117–58, see Tables for classification), was revoked by Ex. Ord. No. 14148, § 2(pp), Jan. 2 ...","quote_truncated":true,"system":"usc","where":"USC 23 U.S.C. 101 note"},"proposal":{"actor":"EO:14148","date":"2025-01-20","mechanism":"revocation","source":{"page_or_item":"23 U.S.C. 101 note; note 'Executive Order No. 14052' [USLM note id idd59924cb-ac5f-11f1-a7aa-9c1372ebafec]; usc23.xml (sha256 43bace6169ed5dfece5d9be6ae7d0f025de6c726347194e04df5f4429fccec9f) in xml_uscAll@119-121.zip","sha256":"c6122974e951003437ece5a998aa7c0b2cdc0f5703dfc78d6135e1fc9e729142","url":"https://uscode.house.gov/download/releasepoints/us/pl/119/121/xml_uscAll@119-121.zip"}},"suggested":false}],"whole_order_end_total":2},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"confirm","ending_or_current_basis":"confirm","opus_media":"n/a","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"2021-11-15","later-events_catalog":"2021-11-15","stage19_causal_queue":"2021-11-15","stage21_crosswalk":"2021-11-15"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:14052","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. Background. The Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act is a \nonce-in-a-generation investment in our Nation’s infrastructure and competi-\ntiveness. It will help rebuild America’s roads, bridges, and rails; expand \naccess to clean drinking water; work to ensure access to high-speed internet \nthroughout the Nation; tackle the climate crisis; advance environmental jus-\ntice; and invest in communities that have too often been left behind. It \nwill accomplish all of this while driving the creation of good-paying union \njobs and growing the economy sustainably and equitably for decades to \ncome. \nCritical to achieving these goals will be the effective implementation of \nthe Act by my Administration, as well as by State, local, Tribal, and territorial \ngovernments.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Implementation Priorities. In implementing the Act, all agencies \n(as described in section 3502(1) of title 44, United States Code, except \nfor the agencies described in section 3502(5) of title 44), shall, as appropriate \nand to the extent consistent with law, prioritize:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) investing public dollars efficiently, working to avoid waste, and focusing \non measurable outcomes for the American people;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) increasing the competitiveness of the United States economy, including \nthrough implementing the Act’s Made-in-America requirements and bol-\nstering United States manufacturing and supply chains;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) improving job opportunities for millions of Americans by focusing \non high labor standards for these jobs, including prevailing wages and the \nfree and fair chance to join a union;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) investing public dollars equitably, including through the Justice40 \nInitiative, which is a Government-wide effort toward a goal that 40 percent \nof the overall benefits from Federal investments in climate and clean energy \nflow to disadvantaged communities;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(d)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec2(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) building infrastructure that is resilient and that helps combat the \ncrisis of climate change; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(e)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec2(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(f) effectively coordinating with State, local, Tribal, and territorial govern-\nments in implementing these critical investments.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(f)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec2(f)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) There is established \nwithin the Executive Office of the President the Infrastructure Implementation \nTask Force (Task Force). The function of the Task Force is to coordinate \neffective implementation of the Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act and \nother related significant infrastructure programs within the executive branch.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Assistant to the President for Economic Policy and Director of \nthe National Economic Council shall serve as Co-Chair of the Task Force.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) There is established within the Executive Office of the President the \nposition of White House Infrastructure Coordinator, who shall serve as Co- \nChair of the Task Force. \nVerDate Sep<11>2014 15:43 Nov 17, 2021 Jkt 256001 PO 00000 Frm 00001 Fmt 4705 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\18NOE0.SGM 18NOE0khammond on DSKJM1Z7X2PROD with PRESDOC\n=== PDF page 2 of 2 ===\n64336 Federal Register / Vol. 86, No. 220 / Thursday, November 18, 2021 / Presidential Documents \n(d) In addition to the Co-Chairs, the Task Force shall consist of the \nfollowing members: \n(i) the Secretary of the Interior; \n(ii) the Secretary of Agriculture; \n(iii) the Secretary of Commerce; \n(iv) the Secretary of Labor; \n(v) the Secretary of Transportation; \n(vi) the Secretary of Energy; \n(vii) the Administrator of the Environmental Protection Agency; \n(viii) the Director of the Office of Management and Budget; \n(ix) the Director of the Office of Personnel Management; \n(x) the Assistant to the President and Director of the Domestic Policy \nCouncil; \n(xi) the Assistant to the President and National Climate Advisor; and \n(xii) the heads of such other executive departments, agencies, and offices \nas the Co-Chairs may from time to time invite to participate. \n(e) The Co-Chairs may coordinate subgroups consisting of Task Force \nmembers or their designees, as appropriate.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Nothing in this order shall be construed \nto impair or otherwise affect: \n(i) the authority granted by law to an executive department or agency, \nor the head thereof; or \n(ii) the functions of the Director of the Office of Management and Budget \nrelating to budgetary, administrative, or legislative proposals.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) This order shall be implemented consistent with applicable law and \nsubject to the availability of appropriations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) This order is not intended to, and does not, create any right or benefit, \nsubstantive or procedural, enforceable at law or in equity by any party \nagainst the United States, its departments, agencies, or entities, its officers, \nemployees, or agents, or any other person.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(c)","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14052#sec4(c)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 64335, PDF pages 1-2","sha256":"8e31c1bfd6f06240ca8ed85e9dce58a629201530fb0b4905c19854ac0670985c","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-11-18/pdf/2021-25286.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 14 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:14052"}
